course: dictionary
lesson: 3917
title: Frolic: play and carefree joy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing or a time). Frolic is both. As a verb, it means to play and run about in a happy, lively way. As a noun, a frolic is a lively, happy game or a fun time. Context shows you which one is meant.
explain: In a story, «The lambs frolic in the spring field» tells you the lambs are running and jumping because they are happy, not because they are working or resting. You can picture it. Frolic is the kind of playing that looks full of joy.
explain: The Rat in The Wind in the Willows hears the reeds sing: «Lest the awe should dwell — And turn your frolic to fret —». Frolic is set against fret, which means worry. The clue is the word turn: happy play can turn into worry. So frolic must mean fun and play.
fact: «Frolic» means to play and run about in a happy, lively way.
fact: As a noun, «a frolic» means lively, happy play or a fun time.
fact: Lambs, puppies and children are often said to frolic, because they are young and full of energy.
fact: «Fret» means worry, so «frolic» and «fret» are very different feelings.
fact: Check a meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The puppies played happily on the beach» still makes sense, so frolic means play.
exercise: «The lambs frolicked in the spring field.» What does frolicked mean? | Walked slowly in a line | Slept under a tree | *Played and ran about happily | Shouted at the farmer
exercise: In «turn your frolic to fret», what does fret mean? | Dance | *Worry | Laugh | Sleep
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The puppies frolic on the beach, happy and lively.» that means playing in a happy way. | lively | *frolic | puppies | beach
test: «The class had a frolic in the park after the test.» In this sentence, what is a frolic? | *A lively, happy time of fun | A sad goodbye | A long, tiring walk | A quiet rest on a bench
test: Which words best describe a child who frolics? | Silent and still | *Playful and joyful | Gloomy and tired | Angry and loud
exam: Ruby says frolic is just another word for walk. Is she right? | Yes, a frolic is a slow walk | *No, frolic means to play in a happy, lively way | No, frolic means to sleep | Yes, it means to sit still
